Skip the KV tiles a workgroup has masked out in tiled flash attention.

The tile path walks every tile of the KV cache for every group of query rows. It stages the K
and V of the tile and scores every cell before the mask is added. With several sequences in one
unified cache a row can only attend to the cells of its own sequence, so most of that work went
into cells whose weight is exp(-inf) = 0. Each row now reads its mask for the tile first, and a
tile that every row of the workgroup has masked with -inf is not staged or scored. For finite K
and V the result is the same: a skipped cell would have added zero.

